<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Æthelthryth</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 636–679</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Etheldreda, Saint Audrey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Æthelthryth, also known as Etheldreda or Audrey, was an East Anglian princess, a daughter of King Anna. Twice married, the second time to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecgfrith-of-northumbria">Ecgfrith of Northumbria</a>, she left her husband to become a nun and in 673 founded a double monastery at Ely, where she was abbess until her death in 679. She became one of the most popular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> saints.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelthryth.jpg" alt="Æthelthryth" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: monk · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St-aethelthryth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
